Z||000000||FieroWenchSE||10-31-2000||08:52 AM||||OKay...I'm going to be replacing the clutch on my 6 cyl. 2.8 86 SE this weekend.  I could use some advice on this...like does the engine have to come completely out, just hoisted up, or is there a way to bypass having to move the engine at all?  Anyone have any ideas?????<P>(and no I'm not doing this all on my own, I'll have two maybe three other Fiero lovers guiding me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||10:56 AM||||Relax. I will be there to help you through it. I can do it in my sleep.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||StuGood||10-31-2000||11:36 AM||||Psst-!  After, TheFiero64's done with yours, point him towards Wichita, and sleepwalk him over here to do mine!||||reg||12
Z||000003||jazer||10-31-2000||04:03 PM||||Check Rodney Dickman's website, I think he has something on removing the clutch without droping the whole sub frame.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||10-31-2000||04:42 PM||||Actually thats Ed Parks that has the info that you are looking for: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top</A> <P>But it isnt all that difficult to remove the cradle.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||04:51 PM||||LOL StuGood, If I am ever in the area I will be glad to help out. I think helping out others is the Fiero way.  <P><B>jazer,</B><BR>I like to do it by dropping the cradle because it is ten times easier to work in the open once you have it out. Then you can inspect the exhaust manifold for cracks and change the plugs and the belt easy at the same time. I would hate to ever find out the manifold had to be replaced and struggle inside the engine compartment to replace it.<BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||EdsB52||10-31-2000||10:16 PM||||Absolutely! I've talked to and corresponded with guys who believe it's easier to just swing down the craddle, but I must disagree. I've tried both and would never perform the latter.||||reg||1
Z||000007||SibERThuG||11-01-2000||12:26 PM||||Hey you guys/girls from Ma, I'm now in Wareham. I need some help. Let me know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Robbie<BR>88' Formula||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroWenchSE||11-01-2000||01:11 PM||||Yeah.....we can take a look at the exhaust manifold but I already know that there is a small crack in it.....that's already going to be fixed..prolly not this weekend but before I get the car on the road.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I still can't beleive that we're going to tow the SE to the back of the house with a ride on lawn mower!!!!!!!!!!!  ||||reg||1
